@tradition crossover-supper
// The crossover supper: every fourth Tuesday (week 3 of the cycle: days 16, 44, 72...), 18:30 in the mess. The plan's
// "crossover breakfast" (06:00) turned round: at 06:00 the night shift goes to bed and nobody can go (events_check:
// nobody went), but at 18:30 the night shift is up (since about 14:00, on at 21:00) and the day shift is off, so the
// day shift's dinner is the night shift's breakfast, at the long tables: the one time they properly meet.
// A meal tradition: ties galley meal=dinner is the `meal` field (the sim engineer eats there instead of at the
// servery). Brennan cooks it and signs the Mail; she's in the galley at that hour, so there's no host.
// No invite either: an invite needs a host (events_check).
// Tuesday week 3 has only Tiles night (Deck 3, 20:00) besides: two that evening, not at once.
k: 457
title: Crossover supper
when: every 4 weeks tuesday week 3
at: 18:30-19:30
min: 20
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat, ids ^3-mess-([1-9]|1[0-6])$
where: 3 pool mess-seat
who: night-owl 60%, lingers-at-meals 60%, everyone 30%
from: brennan
ties: galley meal=dinner dish=crossover-pancakes

== mail
- Crossover supper tomorrow, {time} in the mess. The day shift's dinner is the night shift's breakfast, so there's dinner and pancakes, side by side. Come and meet the people who keep the lights on.

== ask
- Crossover supper tonight. Dinner and pancakes on the same table.   #funny
- Supper with the night shift tonight. I never see them otherwise.
- The crossover's tonight. Best meal of the month.

== here
- Morning! Or evening, for some of us.   #funny
- Pass the syrup, night shift.
- Sit down, there's room at the end.   #warm

== thanks
- You squeeze onto the long table between the two shifts. One lot is having dinner, the other is having breakfast.   #warm

== chatter
- I met half the night shift at the crossover supper. Sleepy, but lovely.   #warm
- At the crossover, the night shift puts syrup on everything. Nobody minds.   #funny
- The crossover's the only time I see my bunkmate awake.   #funny
